 European Medicines Agency; [(accessed on 24 November 2020)]. Paediatric-Use Marketing Authorisations. Available online: https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/human-regulatory/marketing-authorisation/paediatric-medicines/paediatric-use-marketing-authorisations . [ Google Scholar ] 10. Rose K., Grant-Kels J.M. Pediatric melanoma and drug development. Children. 2018;5:43. doi: 10.3390/children5030043. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 11. Rose K. The challenges of pediatric drug development. Curr. Ther. Res. 2019;90:128–134. doi: 10.1016/j.curtheres.2019.01.007. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 12. Rose K., Kopp M.V. Pediatric investigation plans for specific immunotherapy: Questionable contributions to childhood health. Pediatr. Allergy Immunol. 2015;26:695–701. doi: 10.1111/pai.12500. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 13. The European Medicines Agency; [(accessed on 7 November 2019)]. SOP/H/3452 Paediatric Investigation Plan or a Waiver from Start of Procedure to Clock-Stop or PDCO Opinion. Available online: https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/documents/sop/standard-operating-procedure-paediatric-investigation-plan-waiver-start-procedure-clock-stop-pdco_en.pdf . [ Google Scholar ] 14. Tomasi P.A., Egger G.F., Pallidis C., Saint-Raymond A. Enabling development of paediatric medicines in Europe: 10 Years of the EU Paediatric Regulation. Pediatr. Drugs. 2017;19:505–513. doi: 10.1007/s40272-017-0261-1. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 15. The European Medicines Agency; 2010. [(accessed on 20 January 2020)]. Report on the Survey of All Paediatric Uses of Medicinal Products in Europe. Available online: https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/documents/report/report-survey-all-paediatric-uses-medicinal-products-europe_en.pdf . [ Google Scholar ] 16. The European Medicines Agency; [(accessed on 10 November 2020)]. Needs for Pediatric Medicines. Available online: https://www.ema.europa.eu/en/human-regulatory/research-development/paediatric-me